  "created": "2018-05-27T21:55:55.725Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "After doing some testing with the new video sync update I am very happy that it has improved so much and doesn't cause any lag when loading into worlds with videos, especially the ones with many.\n\nHowever, the worlds with many videos in it, will have a white screen until all videos have loaded before it syncs up.\n\nSo worlds with a lot of videos can for some people seem like the video player isn't working.\n\nThere was also the issue, where the video sync only starts for one player, even when multiple people joined into the room at the same time.\n\nWould it be possible to prioritize the synced index to load first and play once loaded, while the rest are loading in the background?\n\nhttps://youtu.be/bGeqCe0y4Wk\n\n00:00 - 07:00 -  Video player only starts for one user. But changing the video index fixes it.\n\n07:00 - 12:00 - Videos are loaded, but white screen so very unsure if the video player starts or not. But instant play when Task Manager shows that Youtube-dl has finished.\n\n12:00 - 16:00 - Still have to wait for all videos to load in the background before anything happens, but syncs up for people with slower connections.\n\n17:00 - 23:00 - Hiding the video panel makes the video stop, only way to get it started again is to have the master client also hide & show the video player.\nAlso, video doesn't sync when it is hidden from you when you load in (intended?) \n\n23:00 - Have to wait for videos to load before anything can be played. (intended?)\n\n\nDon't have much expertise in this, but if it could allow us to play the synced index as soon as it has loaded then load the rest it the background it would be great!",
